            <ArticleTitle>Intestinal perforation caused by larval Eustrongylides (Nematoda: Dioctophymatoidae) in New Jersey.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>648-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two large living nematodes were removed from the peritoneal cavity of a 17-year-old youth complaining of intense abdominal pain in the right lower quadrant. The worms measured 55 and 59 mm in length and were identified as fourth-stage larvae of Eustrongylides. The patient gave a history of swallowing live minnows while fishing.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
